<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">

<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">

    <title>OAuth Security</title>

    <link
        href="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/bootstrap@5.3.3/dist/css/bootstrap.min.css"
        rel="stylesheet">
</head>

<body class="bg-light">

    <div class="container py-5">

        <div class="card shadow">

            <div class="card-body p-5">

                <h1 class="text-center mb-4">
                    OAuth & API Security
                </h1>

                <p class="lead text-center">
                    Understanding secure authentication for APIs
                </p>

                <hr>

                <h3>What is OAuth?</h3>

                <p>
                    OAuth is an authorization framework that allows an
                    application to access protected resources without
                    requiring the user to share their password with the
                    application.
                </p>

                <h3 class="mt-4">How OAuth Works</h3>

                <ol>
                    <li>User requests access to a protected resource.</li>
                    <li>The user authenticates with the authorization server.</li>
                    <li>The authorization server grants authorization.</li>
                    <li>An access token is issued.</li>
                    <li>The application uses the access token to access the API.</li>
                </ol>

                <h3 class="mt-4">Access Token</h3>

                <p>
                    An access token is a credential used by an application
                    to access protected API resources.
                </p>

                <div class="alert alert-info">
                    <strong>Example:</strong>
                    An API request can send an access token using the
                    Authorization header.
                </div>

                <pre class="bg-dark text-white p-3 rounded">
Authorization: Bearer ACCESS_TOKEN
                </pre>

                <h3 class="mt-4">Security Benefits</h3>

                <ul>
                    <li>Passwords are not shared with third-party applications.</li>
                    <li>Access can be limited to specific resources.</li>
                    <li>Tokens can have limited lifetimes.</li>
                    <li>Access can be revoked without changing the user's password.</li>
                </ul>

                <h3 class="mt-4">OAuth in API Applications</h3>

                <p>
                    OAuth is commonly used when applications need secure
                    access to APIs provided by third-party services.
                </p>

                <a href="/students" class="btn btn-primary">
                    Back to Student Dashboard
                </a>

            </div>

        </div>

    </div>

</body>
</html>